  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN267.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">piriviṭai vēṟupaṭṭa talaimaka ḷāṟṟāmai kaṇṭāṟṟāḷākiya tōḻikkut talaimakaḷ colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What SHE said to the confidante who had become unable to bear [it] when seeing the changes in HER [and] the lack of strength in HER who had undergone changes in the time of separation.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN267.1">
        <l><anchor n="1"/>neñcu nekiḻtaru kūṟi yaṉpukalan</l>
        <l>taṟāa vañciṉañ ceytōr viṉaipurintu</l>
        <l>tiṟamvē ṟāka leṉṟeṉ ṟēṟṟi</l>
        <l>yu<supplied>ḷai</supplied>ta lāṉṟici ṉīyē ciṉaipāyn</l>
        <l>tutirtta kōṭai yuṭkuvaru kaṭattiṭai</l>
        <l>verukkaṭi yaṉṉa kuvimuki ḻiruppai</l>
        <l>maruppukkaṭain taṉṉa <supplied>ko</supplied>ḷḷai vā<supplied>ṉ</supplied>pū</l>
        <l>mayirkkā leṇki <supplied>ṉīri</supplied>ṉaṅ kavara</l>
        <l>maippaṭ ṭaṉṉa māmuka mucuviṉam</l>
        <l>paitaṟu neṭuṅkaḻai <supplied>pāy</supplied>tali ṉoyyeṉa</l>
        <l>vetirpaṭu veṇṇel vevvaṟait tāa</l>
        <l>yukirneṟi yōcaiyiṟ poṅkuvaṉa poriyu</l>
        <l>mōṅkal veṟpiṟ curampala viṟantōr</l>
        <l>tāmpaḻi yuṭaiya ralla<supplied>r</supplied> nāḷu</l>
        <l>nayantōrp piṇitta ṟēṟṟār vayaṅkuviṉai</l>
        <l>vāḷē relvaḷai nekiḻnta</l>
        <l>tōḷē tō<supplied>ḻi</supplied> <supplied>ta</supplied>vaṟuṭai yavvē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l>“He who, talking so that [my] heart became soft, mingled with love</l>
        <l>made an unceasing oath, [since] when [is it] that</l>
        <l corresp="1-3">he desires work [and] the issue is different?” so pondering</l>
        <l corresp="4a-c">you please stop wailing.</l>
        <l corresp="13">He who traversed many deserts with high mountains,</l>
        <l corresp="4d-5">where, in the dreadful wilderness, with the west wind that rushes at the branches [and] strips off [their flowers],</l>
        <l corresp="8">while the big group of bears with furry legs seize</l>
        <l corresp="7">as [their] plunder the white flowers that grow like horns,</l>
        <l corresp="6">of the mahua tree with piling buds that are like the wild cat’s feet,</l>
        <l corresp="9">because the horde of langurs, [their] faces black as if made up with kajal,</l>
        <l corresp="10">jump on the sapless long bamboo [poles], suddenly,</l>
        <l corresp="11">the white paddy falling from the bamboo spreads on the hot rock</l>
        <l corresp="12">[and its] popping bits are fried with a sound like fingernails clicking,</l>
        <l corresp="14">the blame is not his. Daily</l>
        <l corresp="17">it is the shoulders, friend, that are at fault,</l>
        <l corresp="16">on which the bright bangles beautiful with light have become loose,</l>
        <l corresp="15">of glowing craftmanship, [belonging to a woman] who does not make sure to bind the one who loves [her].</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
